{"entryId":"2404","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:2404:1","sourceSha256":"4e17785a332471fbc3a083280b1b2d556efb7bc28ec48aa38d27b4454b5ec2e7","englishSha256":"4b4f7c84bfff6e8b1988496ccbac3c46bffcbfd37c852456d32772ba6a57fbec","citations":[{"id":"2404:1:link-01","he":[72,88],"en":[137,147],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_67b.18"},"reference":"Niddah 67b:18","assessment":"Rav Adda recounts the episode of the exilarch’s wife. Rav Naḥman bar Yitzḥak goes to appease her.","evidence":[{"reference":"Niddah 67b:18","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_67b.18"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"2404:1:link-02","he":[89,105],"en":[152,168],"target":{"entry":217,"paragraph":1},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 217:1","assessment":"The related entry explicitly supplies both the textual setting and Heilprin’s expanded explanation of the quarrel.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 217:1","target":{"entry":217,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]},{"id":"2404:1:link-03","he":[107,154],"en":[170,191],"target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%A9%D7%95%22%D7%AA_%D7%9E%D7%94%D7%A8%D7%A9%22%D7%9C/%D7%A1%D7%99%D7%9E%D7%9F_%D7%95"},"reference":"Responsa Maharshal 6","assessment":"Responsum 6 explicitly calls Rav Naḥman his son-in-law and makes the quarrel be between the woman and her husband. Niddah names Rav Naḥman bar Yitzḥak without giving that relationship.","evidence":[{"reference":"Responsa Maharshal 6","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%A9%D7%95%22%D7%AA_%D7%9E%D7%94%D7%A8%D7%A9%22%D7%9C/%D7%A1%D7%99%D7%9E%D7%9F_%D7%95"},"witness":"Responsa Maharshal, §6, Hebrew Wikisource transcription"},{"reference":"Niddah 67b","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_67b"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Rav Adda recounts the episode of the exilarch’s wife. Rav Naḥman bar Yitzḥak goes to appease her.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The related entry explicitly supplies both the textual setting and Heilprin’s expanded explanation of the quarrel.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The Bavli and Heilprin’s associated Adda article both make the woman the wife of Abba Mari. The existing English pronoun suggests the wrong husband.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Responsum 6 explicitly calls Rav Naḥman his son-in-law and makes the quarrel be between the woman and her husband. Niddah names Rav Naḥman bar Yitzḥak without giving that relationship.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Niddah 67b:18","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_67b.18"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 217:1","target":{"entry":217,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Niddah 67b","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_67b"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 217:1","target":{"entry":217,"paragraph":1},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"},{"reference":"Responsa Maharshal 6","target":{"url":"https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%A9%D7%95%22%D7%AA_%D7%9E%D7%94%D7%A8%D7%A9%22%D7%9C/%D7%A1%D7%99%D7%9E%D7%9F_%D7%95"},"witness":"Responsa Maharshal, §6, Hebrew Wikisource transcription"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
